1
00:00:00,893 --> 00:00:03,703
"Do you have Leonard's
email address?"

2
00:00:06,265 --> 00:00:07,265
(Sheldon:)And...

3
00:00:07,433 --> 00:00:09,713
"Never mind, I found it."

4
00:00:11,804 --> 00:00:13,754
(Amy:)I can't believe
he picked you over me.

5
00:00:13,906 --> 00:00:16,476
(Howard:)You don't want to read a paper
by some old has-been

6
00:00:16,642 --> 00:00:19,992
(Howard:)who hasn't done
any real science in decades.

7
00:00:20,146 --> 00:00:21,626
(Raj:)Yeah, it's nothing to cry about.

8
00:00:21,781 --> 00:00:24,261
(Sheldon:)Sheldon Cooper does not cry.

9
00:00:24,383 --> 00:00:26,293
(Howard:)It's true. You'd rust.

10
00:00:32,158 --> 00:00:34,328
(Sheldon:)And to think I idolized that man.

11
00:00:34,494 --> 00:00:35,994
(Sheldon:)And why?

12
00:00:36,162 --> 00:00:38,942
(Sheldon:)At the end of the day he's just
another Hollywood phony.

13
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:42,446
(Amy:)Is it really worth
getting upset about?

14
00:00:42,602 --> 00:00:44,172
(Sheldon:)They say don't meet your heroes.

15
00:00:44,337 --> 00:00:47,147
(Sheldon:)Don't peek behind
that curtain of fame and celebrity,

16
00:00:47,306 --> 00:00:50,186
(Sheldon:)because if you do,

17
00:00:50,343 --> 00:00:52,253
(Sheldon:)degenerate carnival folk.

18
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:56,280
(Amy:)Come on,
he's a retired kids show host.

19
00:00:56,449 --> 00:00:59,659
(Sheldon:)That's even worse.
Using the sweet candy of science

20
00:00:59,819 --> 00:01:03,019
(Sheldon:)to trick children into loving him.

